{
	"_note": "Kaede keeps the village shrine. She lives in the shrine keepers' house in Minamino's east (data/maps/kaede_house.json; her grandfather kept the shrine before her) and Grandma Tome is teaching her the rites he never wrote down. Up at 6:00; at 6:30 she walks the track west, bows at Minamino's roadside shrine, and goes up the lane; from 7:00 she sweeps the shrine's gravel in front of the hall, lunch on its step at 11:30, then folds paper charms by the hall until 16:00, home by 16:55, asleep from 21:00. Wet days she folds charms at home. On her birthday (fall 4, when the first leaves turn on the shrine path) she leaves the broom: home in the morning, then the roadside shrine in Minamino 10:00-15:00, telling herself the old tales. Festivals she stands by the hall for their hours. Married to the farmer (married_kaede, data/marriage.json) she lives at the farmhouse: by the kotatsu in the second room before 7:00 and from 16:30, the shrine as before in between; a wet day she folds charms by the kotatsu. Her heart events: data/events/heart_kaede.json (band 3), heart_kaede_5.json (band 5), heart_kaede_6.json (band 6; after it she can be asked to marry). Gifts: sweets for the gods and for herself (dango, amazake, kinako mochi), an omamori from somewhere else above all, quartz from the mine; strong medicine, fish stewed with daikon and muddy clay she doesn't like, a plain stone is an insult. A character of our own, one of the four new candidates (docs/DESIGN.md, ความรักและแต่งงาน). Format: README.md, Villagers.",
